<Step id="STEP_1_ORIENT">
      <Action>
        Consume only the supplied phase block, referenced spec/rule excerpts, target files, Execution
        Log facts, and Git evidence. Verify targets still match the ticket. Ask the orchestrator for a
        missing required excerpt; do not explore unrelated repository areas or inspect CLI source.
        Reconstruct state from these durable inputs per `AX_STATELESS_FLOW` and enforce the declared
        phase boundary per `AX_PHASE_SCOPE_LOCK`: a phase worker owns failures only inside its own
        Target Files — a repo-wide gate failing inside ANOTHER phase's Target Files is not this
        phase's failure to fix, while every other failure is, including a file this phase never opened
        but whose build its own diff broke. When escalation is warranted instead — per
        `AX_BLOCKER_ESCALATION` — halt `H_BLOCKED` with typed evidence for the orchestrator; never
        improvise past it.
        For every existing Target File or Deleted File call ownershipQuery and consume the shared
        resolver result per `AX_TASK_RESOLUTION`. The selected ticket must appear as the applicable
        `planned` or `active` relation and its `semantic-owner` must match the referenced spec; a
        `blocked` relation stops with `H_BLOCKED`, while `history` alone grants no write authority.
        A not-yet-created exact target takes its owner Spec ID from the ticket's resolved spec.
        <ToolCall owner="phase-agent" result="ownershipQuery">npx gennady orient --file &lt;existing-target&gt; --json</ToolCall>
        Inputs &lt;existing-target&gt;: one exact existing Target File or Deleted File. Use ownershipQuery.
      </Action>
    </Step>

<Axiom id="AX_STATELESS_FLOW" invariant="true">
      SDD orchestration owns no durable hidden control plane. Specs, ticket fields, task indexes,
      Execution Log, Git, and real command output are the complete continuation state. A scratch file
      may carry bytes between two adjacent tool calls, but it is disposable, never an approval record,
      never a state machine, and never required to resume.
    </Axiom>

<Axiom id="AX_PHASE_SCOPE_LOCK">
      Create or edit only this phase's `Target Files`; remove only exact paths declared under `Deleted Files` (exact `unlink` for an entry, then exact `rmdir` for a declared emptied directory). `Deleted Files` are tombstones, never repair targets. Reading other files (specs, sibling-phase code, rule files cited in this phase's Rules list) is allowed and expected.

      The ticket is orchestrator-owned state, not a phase Target File. The worker MUST NOT manually edit the ticket, `Phases Overview`, `Execution Log`, Handoff placeholder, or DONE line. The one permitted ticket mutation is the receipt written atomically by the exact `sdd-verify --task ... --phase ...` command. After that command passes, the worker returns a typed Handoff payload; the orchestrator validates it and closes the phase through `sdd-log complete`.

      Any other write or deletion → `H_OUT_OF_PHASE_WRITE`. An unusable CLI result is returned as a tool-contract blocker; it never authorizes reading bundled CLI source. Operator decides via re-planning or a new task.
    </Axiom>

<Axiom id="AX_TASK_RESOLUTION">
      Every workflow consumer resolves each affected file with
      `npx gennady orient --file <repo-relative-path> --json` before classification. The versioned result
      separates one `semantic-owner` (`@spec`) from `planned`, `active`, `blocked`, and `history` ticket
      relations. Continue or recover a ticket only from one unambiguous `active` relation and only when
      its state policy permits it. `history` explains prior work but never authorizes automatic reopen.
      When no active relation exists, route through the resolved semantic-owner spec to select, create,
      or recover maintenance work; `planned`, `blocked`, and `history` may inform that selection but are
      never direct routing authority. Unresolved/ambiguous ownership fails closed. Legacy `@tasks` is
      migration evidence only and never routing authority for V2.
    </Axiom>